# Versioning and GitHub Release

Do **not** commit `release/`. Binaries stay gitignored and go to GitHub Release assets.

`package.json` `version` is the source of truth. Tag = `v` + version (`0.1.0` → `v0.1.0`).

When the user says «ورژن بده» / «release» / «publish», run this flow. Ask patch vs minor vs major only if they did not specify. Default to `patch`.

## Every new version

1. `npm run bump-version -- patch` (or `minor` / `major` / `1.2.3`).
   Updates `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `src/shared/app-version.ts`, `src/extension/manifest.json`.
2. `npm run dist` — writes versioned files into `release/`.
3. Commit **only** the version bump (never `release/`).
4. Working tree must be clean, then `npm run publish-release`
   — tags `vX.Y.Z`, pushes, creates the GitHub Release, uploads:
   - `MYs Chapar-X.Y.Z-arm64.dmg`
   - `MYs Chapar-X.Y.Z-win.zip`
   - `mychapar-linux-X.Y.Z.zip`
   - `MYs Chapar-X.Y.Z-chrome.zip`
   - `MYs Chapar-X.Y.Z-vscode.vsix`

If `release/` already has all five files for the **current** `package.json` version and that tag is not fully published, skip bump/dist and only run `publish-release`.
